      "writtenOn": "2022-10-04T02:43:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using the default task queue seems like it might cause some problems since we run that at minimum priority, so signals might change state much later than expected if other threads are running.\n\nIt doesn\u0027t seem like the emulator can use timestamps instead (because it may need to trigger interrupts so it needs to run code after a delay rather than simply measuring the passage of time), but it may be better to define a work queue internal to the emulator which can run at a high priority.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 384,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 384,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "0041f9bddad1bc6b75aa224ed8c10726ffdd0fa9",
